-- title:
--   Existence of a separating transcendental element on a curve
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $F$ be fields with $F$ a $K$-algebra, $K$ perfect, and $F$ essentially of finite type over $K$, and assume $F$ is a curve over $K$ in the sense of the predicate `IsCurveOver`: namely (i) $F/K$ has principal divisors, in that for every $f \in F$ with $f \neq 0$ there is a divisor $D$ on $F/K$ with $D(v) = \operatorname{ord}_v(f)$ at every place $v$ and $\deg D = 0$, where a place is a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $K$, distinct from $F$ itself, and a principal ideal ring; (ii) for every such place $v$ the residue field of the corresponding valuation subring is a finite $K$-module; and (iii) the module of Kähler differentials $\Omega_{F/K}$ is free of rank one over $F$. Then there exists $t \in F$ which is transcendental over $K$ and such that $F$ is finite-dimensional over the intermediate field $K\langle t\rangle$ generated by $t$ and is separable over $K\langle t\rangle$; that is, $F/K(t)$ is a finite separable extension.
--
--   This is the existence of a separating element (equivalently, a separating transcendence basis of size one) for a curve over a perfect field, the direction of the standard characterisation of algebraic function fields in one variable that produces a rational subfield $K(t)$ over which $F$ is finite separable. It supplies the $K(t)$-tower presentation used throughout the development, and is invoked by the results on divisors, genus, residues and component charts built on `IsCurveOver`.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_IsCurveOver_exists_separating_transcendental.lean

import Mathlib
